  "rules_provenance": null,
  "source_rule_excerpts": [
   "Receiver operating characteristic analysis was used to determine these cut-off scores using the Leeds Dependence Questionnaire and the Self-Report Questionnaire (Schlesinger et al., 2007). For the AOD subscale, a score of 10 provided a high specificity of 86% and a moderate sensitivity of 65%. In other words, the AOD subscale is more accurate at correctly identifying low risk clients. Conversely, this subscale is weaker at correctly classifying high risk clients, therefore high scorers should be viewed with less confidence that their classification is correct."
  ],
